.TH YTDA "1" "December 2025" "ytda 202606040840-git" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytda \- Video downloader and MP3 converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytda
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,COMMAND\/\fR] [\fI\,URL|ID|FILE\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytda
is a script for downloading videos and converting them to MP3 audio format. It uses yt-dlp/youtube-dl to download videos and extract audio tracks.
.PP
The script is useful for downloading audio from video sources.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mp3, aac, flac, m4a, opus, vorbis, wav
Download audio and convert it to that format
.TP
.B yta, ytda
Download audio and convert it to mp3
.TP
.B nightcore
Download Nightcore audio as mp3 into ~/Music/Nightcore
.TP
.B playlist CHANNEL
Save a channel's playlists to ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/channels/CHANNEL.txt
.PP
With no command the audio is converted to mp3. URLs may be given as arguments, as a file containing URLs, or on stdin. A bare video ID is expanded with YTDA_DEFAULT_URL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display help message with usage information and available options
.TP
.BR \-\-config
Generate or regenerate user configuration file with default settings
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show script version information and exit
.TP
.BR \-\-options
Display all available command-line options
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug mode with verbose output and command tracing (set -x)
.TP
.BR \-\-no-color
Disable colorized output for plain text display
.TP
.BR \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Set the working directory
.TP
.BR \-\-channel " " \fINAME\fR
Playlist type used by the playlist command (default: channels)
.TP
.BR \-\-username " " \fIUSER\fR ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASS\fR ", " \-\-netrc
Credentials passed to yt-dlp
.TP
.BR \-\-silent
Reduce output
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ytda https://youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID
Download video and convert to MP3
.TP
.B ytda "https://example.com/video"
Download audio from video URL
.SH FILE NAMES
Titles are cleaned before the file name and tags are written, so "Never Gonna Give You Up (Official Video) (4K Remaster)" is saved as "Never Gonna Give You Up", and a trailing " - Official Video" or " | Official Audio" is dropped too. Official versions are downloaded before live ones (see YTDA_PREFER_OFFICIAL), so when two videos clean to the same name the official one keeps it and the later one is skipped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/settings.conf
User configuration file for ytda preferences
.TP
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/cookies.txt
Optional Netscape-format cookies file passed to yt-dlp with --cookies (override with YTDA_COOKIE_FILE)
.TP
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/archive/
Lists of downloaded URLs; yt-dlp's own archive is ytdl.txt
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YTDA_COOKIE_FILE
Netscape-format cookies file (default: ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/cookies.txt). ytda warns when it is missing, lacks the Netscape header, or has no youtube.com cookies
.TP
.B YTDA_JS_RUNTIME
JavaScript runtime for YouTube (deno, node, bun or quickjs). Detected automatically when unset; yt-dlp only enables deno on its own
.TP
.B YTDA_MAX_ERRORS
Failures allowed in one playlist before the rest of it is skipped (default: 10, 0 disables)
.TP
.B YTDA_BIN_DIR
Directory the yt-dlp binary is installed to, overriding the root/sudo detection
.SH COOKIES
YouTube rotates the account cookies of any browser session that stays open, which invalidates an exported cookies file. When that happens yt-dlp reports that the cookies are no longer valid, ytda prints a notice, and downloads may fail with a bot check or return only a low quality stream. To export cookies that do not rotate, use yt-dlp's recommended method:
.IP 1. 3
Open a new private (incognito) window with no other private tabs, and sign in to YouTube.
.IP 2. 3
In that same tab, open https://www.youtube.com/robots.txt
.IP 3. 3
Export the youtube.com cookies with a cookies.txt browser extension, save them as
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytda/cookies.txt
(or the file named by YTDA_COOKIE_FILE), then close the private window. Never open that session in a browser again.
.PP
Do not use \fB\-\-cookies-from-browser\fR: it reads the regular browser profile, whose cookies keep rotating. yt-dlp rewrites the cookies file on exit and drops cookies YouTube has invalidated, so a stale file keeps shrinking.
.PP
Cookies are only needed for private playlists, age-restricted videos and members-only content. Using an account can lead to a temporary or permanent ban, so keep download volume modest or use a throwaway account.
.TP
.B YTDA_STRIP_TITLE
Set to "no" to keep tags such as (Official Video), [4K] and (Live) in titles (default: yes). Set it in settings.conf, which takes precedence over the environment
.TP
.B YTDA_STRIP_WORDS
Regex alternation of the noise words (default: official|music|video|audio|lyrics?|lyric|visuali[sz]er|remaster(?:ed)?|hd|hq|4k|8k|1080p|720p|live|explicit|full). Only a bracket made up entirely of these words, and optionally years, is removed, so (Live Forever) and (Live at Wembley) are kept
.TP
.B YTDA_PREFER_OFFICIAL
Set to "no" to download titles in the order yt-dlp returns them (default: yes). With yes, titles tagged Live are held back with --match-filters and fetched in a second pass, only for the URLs that had some, so "Artist - Song" is saved before "Artist - Song (Live)". Set it in settings.conf
.TP
.B YTDA_LIVE_REGEX
Python regex that marks a title as live (default: a bracket containing the word live, or a trailing "- Live"). Titles it matches are downloaded last
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
No URL given, or a download failed (the number of failed downloads is returned)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Downloads and converts to MP3
.IP \(bu 2
Supports multiple video sites
.IP \(bu 2
Per-video errors (unavailable, private) are skipped and the run continues. Errors that repeat for every URL (bot check, HTTP 403, HTTP 429) stop the run with a hint
.IP \(bu 2
Requires internet connection
.IP \(bu 2
If yt-dlp is missing it is installed from the official release to /usr/local/bin for root or a user who can sudo, otherwise to ~/.local/bin and checked against the published SHA2-256SUMS. The standalone build matching the OS, CPU and libc is used (yt-dlp_linux for glibc, yt-dlp_musllinux for musl, yt-dlp_macos); other platforms need Python 3.11+ for the zipimport build. An existing yt-dlp that fails \fB--version\fR is reported and never overwritten
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
yt-dlp/youtube-dl - Video downloader
.IP \(bu 2
ffmpeg - Audio conversion
.RE
